{
  "description": "Cross-SDK vectors for the auth_context claim mappers (Go FromXClaims, TypeScript fromX, Python from_x). Each case runs the same verified claims and overrides through the named helper (any provider other than workos, clerk and auth0 uses the generic OIDC helper with that slug); the JSON every SDK sends must equal expect exactly. Rules the vectors pin: contact verification comes from token claims only for Auth0 (email_verified and phone_number_verified), from overrides for every provider; a NumericDate is written as RFC 3339 in whole UTC seconds, the fraction truncated; string claims split on whitespace (OAuth scope, RFC 6749 section 3.3), and Clerk permissions also on commas; Clerk's role is one slug; Clerk never sends issued_at from iat (a 60-second refresh clock; session age is the session_created_at override); Auth0 amr lists every method except pwd, and an amr of only pwd sends no mfa; the first-class adapters always send impersonated, false included; an override replaces the mapped value, false included. Unknown, mistyped, out-of-range and out-of-contract claims map to absent, never to a stronger assurance: a case with \"error\": true must be refused (a TypeError, ValueError or the language's equivalent) because issuer or subject is missing or invalid or the provider slug is not a lowercase slug; Clerk fva counts only a numeric second factor from 0 to ten years of minutes; Auth0 amr counts only an array of strings; a time string must be RFC 3339; and token claims never set assurance_level.",
